IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`
IMPORT `euca-s203-period`
IMPORT `euca-s203-indicators`
IMPORT `euca-s202-account`

-- Tests for section 202(b) and (c): the size of the extended compensation account, the high
-- unemployment period, and the stop on extended compensation paid on an interstate claim.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text before the file was run; each case
-- says what the hand calculation was. Money is in dollars. Nothing here is a rule of the Act.

§ `Tests: section 202(b), (c), the account and interstate claims`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN total IS A NUMBER
      weeklyAmount IS A NUMBER
      regularPaid IS A NUMBER
      reduces IS A BOOLEAN
      additional IS A NUMBER
      highUnemployment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Account facts`
`in the account tests, an account of` total weeklyAmount regularPaid reduces additional highUnemployment MEANS
    `Account facts` WITH
        `total regular compensation payable during the benefit year, including dependents' allowances` IS total
        `average weekly benefit amount` IS weeklyAmount
        `regular compensation paid or deemed paid during the benefit year` IS regularPaid
        `the State law reduces the account by additional compensation paid` IS reduces
        `additional compensation paid or deemed paid for prior weeks in the benefit year that did not begin in an extended benefit period` IS additional
        `the week begins in a high unemployment period` IS highUnemployment

GIVEN wouldBePayable IS A BOOLEAN
      ebpInClaimState IS A BOOLEAN
      earlierWeeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Interstate claim`
`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` wouldBePayable ebpInClaimState earlierWeeks MEANS
    `Interstate claim` WITH
        `extended compensation would but for the cessation rule have been payable for the week pursuant to an interstate claim under the interstate benefit payment plan` IS wouldBePayable
        `an extended benefit period is in effect for the week in the State where the claim was filed` IS ebpInClaimState
        `earlier weeks for which extended compensation was payable pursuant to the interstate claim from the account` IS earlierWeeks

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
      first IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Total unemployment reading`
`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` rate first second MEANS
    `Total unemployment reading` WITH
        `average rate of total unemployment (seasonally adjusted) for the most recent 3 months for which data for all States are published` IS rate
        `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the first preceding calendar year` IS first
        `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the second preceding calendar year` IS second
        `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the third preceding calendar year` IS 0
        `the State law adopts the alternative trigger` IS FALSE
        `date from which the State law adopts the three-year comparison option` IS NOTHING

§§ `202(b)(2): the weekly benefit amount`

-- 350 of regular compensation for total unemployment plus 50 of dependents' allowances: 400.
#ASSERT `the weekly benefit amount for a week` 350 50 EQUALS 400

§§ `202(b)(1): the least of three amounts`

-- Total payable 10,000, weekly benefit amount 400, paid 10,000.
-- (A) 50 per cent of 10,000 = 5,000. (B) 13 x 400 = 5,200. (C) 39 x 400 - 10,000 = 15,600 - 10,000 = 5,600.
#ASSERT `the amount under section 202(b)(1)(A)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the amount under section 202(b)(1)(B)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 5200
#ASSERT `the amount under section 202(b)(1)(C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 5600
#ASSERT `the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 5000
-- Total payable 12,000, paid 12,000: (A) 6,000; (B) 5,200; (C) 15,600 - 12,000 = 3,600. Least: 3,600.
#ASSERT `the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 12000 400 12000 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 3600
-- Total payable 20,800, paid 4,000: (A) 10,400; (B) 5,200; (C) 15,600 - 4,000 = 11,600. Least: 5,200.
#ASSERT `the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 20800 400 4000 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 5200

§§ `202(b)(3)(A): the figures in a high unemployment period`

-- Total payable 10,000, paid 10,000: (A) 80 per cent = 8,000. (B) 20 x 400 = 8,000. (C) 46 x 400 - 10,000 = 18,400 - 10,000 = 8,400. Least: 8,000.
#ASSERT `the amount under section 202(b)(1)(A)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 TRUE) EQUALS 8000
#ASSERT `the amount under section 202(b)(1)(B)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 TRUE) EQUALS 8000
#ASSERT `the amount under section 202(b)(1)(C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 TRUE) EQUALS 8400
#ASSERT `the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 TRUE) EQUALS 8000
-- Total payable 12,000, paid 12,000: (A) 9,600; (B) 8,000; (C) 18,400 - 12,000 = 6,400. Least: 6,400.
#ASSERT `the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` (`in the account tests, an account of` 12000 400 12000 FALSE 0 TRUE) EQUALS 6400

§§ `202(b)(1), closing words: reduction by additional compensation`

-- If the State law so provides, 700 of earlier additional compensation reduces 5,000 to 4,300.
#ASSERT `the amount the extended compensation account must hold` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 TRUE 700 FALSE) EQUALS 4300
-- If it does not, the account stays 5,000.
#ASSERT `the amount the extended compensation account must hold` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 700 FALSE) EQUALS 5000

§§ `202(b)(1) and (2): how many whole weeks the account covers`

-- 5,000 at 400 a week: 12.5, so 12 whole weeks.
#ASSERT `the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) 400 EQUALS JUST 12
-- 5,000 at 500 a week: 10.
#ASSERT `the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) 500 EQUALS JUST 10
-- 3,600 at 400 a week: 9.
#ASSERT `the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` (`in the account tests, an account of` 12000 400 12000 FALSE 0 FALSE) 400 EQUALS JUST 9
-- 4,300 at 400 a week: 10.75, so 10.
#ASSERT `the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 TRUE 700 FALSE) 400 EQUALS JUST 10
-- A weekly amount of 0 cannot be divided into: the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` (`in the account tests, an account of` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Total payable 16,000, paid 16,000: (C) 15,600 - 16,000 = -400 is the least; no weeks are covered.
#ASSERT `the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` (`in the account tests, an account of` 16000 400 16000 FALSE 0 FALSE) 400 EQUALS JUST 0

§§ `202(b)(3)(B): the high unemployment period`

#ASSERT `the percentage substituted in section 202(b)(3)(B)` EQUALS 8
-- 8 against 7 and 7: 8 equals 8, and 110 per cent of 7 is 7.7: the week is "on" for this purpose. The State law's adoption of the trigger is not asked.
#ASSERT (`the reading for the high unemployment period` (Date 13 1 2013) (`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` 8 7 7))'s `State on indicator`
-- 7.9 against 7 and 7 is under 8: not on.
#ASSERT NOT ((`the reading for the high unemployment period` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` 7.9 7 7))'s `State on indicator`)
#ASSERT (`the reading for the high unemployment period` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` 7.9 7 7))'s `week beginning` EQUALS Date 6 1 2013

`in the account tests, readings for the high unemployment period` MEANS
    LIST (`the reading for the high unemployment period` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` 7.9 7 7)),
         (`the reading for the high unemployment period` (Date 13 1 2013) (`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` 8 7 7)),
         (`the reading for the high unemployment period` (Date 20 1 2013) (`in the account tests, a total unemployment reading of` 8 7 7))

-- The first "on" week is 13 January 2013; the hypothetical period begins the third week after, 3 February 2013, and has no end yet.
#ASSERT `the week begins in a high unemployment period` (Date 3 2 2013) (`the extended benefit period that follows the readings` (`in the account tests, readings for the high unemployment period`) NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT `the week begins in a high unemployment period` (Date 24 2 2013) (`the extended benefit period that follows the readings` (`in the account tests, readings for the high unemployment period`) NOTHING TRUE)
-- 27 January 2013 is before it begins.
#ASSERT NOT (`the week begins in a high unemployment period` (Date 27 1 2013) (`the extended benefit period that follows the readings` (`in the account tests, readings for the high unemployment period`) NOTHING TRUE))
-- No period would be in effect: no high unemployment period.
#ASSERT NOT (`the week begins in a high unemployment period` (Date 3 2 2013) NOTHING)

§§ `202(c): interstate claims in a State with no extended benefit period`

-- The first 2 weeks payable on the claim are exempt: 0 or 1 earlier weeks means this is the first or the second.
#ASSERT `the week is one of the first 2 weeks payable pursuant to the interstate claim` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `the week is one of the first 2 weeks payable pursuant to the interstate claim` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`the week is one of the first 2 weeks payable pursuant to the interstate claim` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 2))
-- Third week, no extended benefit period in the claim State, would otherwise have been payable: payment is not made.
#ASSERT `payment of extended compensation is not made for the week under section 202(c)(1)` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 2)
-- Second week: exempt.
#ASSERT NOT (`payment of extended compensation is not made for the week under section 202(c)(1)` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 1))
-- An extended benefit period is in effect in the claim State: no stop.
#ASSERT NOT (`payment of extended compensation is not made for the week under section 202(c)(1)` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE TRUE 5))
-- Not payable in any event: nothing to stop.
#ASSERT NOT (`payment of extended compensation is not made for the week under section 202(c)(1)` (`in the account tests, an interstate claim of` FALSE FALSE 5))
-- (c)(3): section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code does not apply to a denial required by the subsection.
#ASSERT `section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code does not apply to the denial` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code does not apply to the denial` FALSE)
